From: Jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] CompositorShadowNode: fixing a light to a shadow map invalidates the cached light-list build

WHY (Jahshaka lane E2, the lamp-map cache, 2026-09-12 — measured)

`CompositorShadowNode::buildClosestLightList` rebuilds a node's light list at
most once per (camera, compositor frame): `mLastCamera == newCamera &&
mLastFrame == currentFrameCount` returns early. That build is the ONLY place
`mNumActiveShadowMapCastingLights` is computed.

`setLightFixedToShadowMap` writes `mShadowMapCastingLights[lightIdx]` without
touching that count. Upstream's own use (the StaticShadowMaps sample) fixes its
lights once, before anything renders, so the two are never out of step. A host
that re-assigns fixed lights PER FRAME — a lamp-map cache — is out of step for
every pass that runs between the assignment and the node's next build, and such
a pass exists whenever a reflection probe captures in the same compositor frame
in which the node last built (Ogre's PCC captures from outside the render
phase, so the frame counter has not advanced).

The two disagreeing numbers are both read by Hlms in the same pass:

  * `hlms_num_shadow_map_lights` = getNumActiveShadowCastingLights() +
    (pssmSplits - 1)                                  [OgreHlms.cpp:3269-3273]
  * the pass's shadow-casting light counts per type, walked straight off
    `getShadowCastingLights()`                        [OgreHlms.cpp:3493-3505]

Measured on a probe capture: declared = 3, needed = 4, nodeActive = 1,
held = [dynamic directional][static spot][empty]. The shader falls out of the
static-branching path and references `hlms_shadowmap3` against three declared
maps: "'hlms_shadowmap3' : undeclared identifier", the PBS pixel shader does not
compile, and on a cold shader cache the null cache entry that leaves behind
crashes HlmsDiskCache::Pso when the disk cache is saved.

THE FIX: dropping the cached camera makes the next `buildClosestLightList`
rebuild, which is the only place the count can be brought back in step with the
array. Costs one extra light-list build after an assignment CHANGES (nothing at
rest — the host only calls this when the slot's lamp really changed) and is a
no-op for upstream's own usage, which fixes its lights before the first frame.

diff --git a/OgreMain/src/Compositor/OgreCompositorShadowNode.cpp b/OgreMain/src/Compositor/OgreCompositorShadowNode.cpp
index 911e768d9..50efc8f74 100644
--- a/OgreMain/src/Compositor/OgreCompositorShadowNode.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/Compositor/OgreCompositorShadowNode.cpp
@@ -924,6 +924,20 @@ namespace Ogre
         mShadowMapCastingLights[lightIdx].light = light;
         mShadowMapCastingLights[lightIdx].isStatic = light != 0;
         mShadowMapCastingLights[lightIdx].isDirty = true;
+
+        // THE CACHED BUILD NO LONGER DESCRIBES THIS NODE (Jahshaka).
+        // buildClosestLightList rebuilds at most once per (camera, compositor
+        // frame) and it is what computes mNumActiveShadowMapCastingLights.
+        // Hlms declares hlms_num_shadow_map_lights from that COUNT
+        // (OgreHlms.cpp:3269) but counts the pass's shadow-casting lights from
+        // THIS ARRAY (OgreHlms.cpp:3493-3505), so a light fixed after the node
+        // has already built for the current frame makes the two disagree: the
+        // generated PBS shader then references hlms_shadowmap<N> beyond what it
+        // declared and fails to compile. Dropping the cached camera forces the
+        // next build, which is the only place the count can be brought back in
+        // step.
+        mLastCamera = 0;
+        mLastFrame = std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max();
     }
     //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     void CompositorShadowNode::setStaticShadowMapDirty( size_t shadowMapIdx, bool includeLinked )
